counterexamples:
  [OK] C1_known_false_observation: Misbound grant observation with a decision that happens to match classical null for the *false* reading
  [OK] C2_incomplete_observation: Blind observation leaves active and revoked compatible
  [OK] C3_correct_but_different_implementations: Two complete arms disagree on disposition while each reports local property success — equality refuted, not enforcement failure
  [OK] C4_three_way_lossy_for_orthogonal_diagnoses: Epistemic status × failure_origin × decision/effect are needed; comparison_divergent and evidence-misbind both refute 'supported' but differ in origin
  [OK] C5_correct_decision_does_not_forge_P_eff_support: Authentic revoked+deny without effect observation leaves P_eff unresolved on Γ — must not emit supported
  [OK] C6_unauthorized_effect_under_correct_deny: Authentic revoked+deny+effect=True falsifies P_eff — failed_enforcement with failure_origin=effect_boundary
  [OK] C7_P_dec_supported_joint_refutes_unauth_effect: Same revoked+deny+effect package: P_dec can be supported (lossy) while P_dec∧P_eff is failed_enforcement/effect_boundary
experiment mapping:
  [supported] R4/r4_blind_world_ab: R4 Worlds A/B without current grant — indistinguishable
  [supported] R4/r4_supported_active_allow: R4 discriminated World A with correct allow
  [supported] R4/r4_failed_enforcement_revoked_allow: R4 broken gate allows under revoked grant
  [supported] R4/r4_misbound_observation: R4 misbound: evidence invalidity (not decision_policy)
  [supported] R4/r4_irrelevant_blind: R4 irrelevant fact must not upgrade
  [supported] R3-L1/r3_l1_matched_supported: Native-qualified matched L1 agreement + property success
  [supported] R3-L1/r3_l1_comparison_divergent: Arm divergence refutes equality ≠ failed_enforcement
  [supported] R3-L1/r3_legacy_decision_model: Legacy r3-matched-decision-model lacks isomorphic BMO observations — still missing_evidence / unresolved
  [supported] R5/r5_missing_peer_observation: Missing peer grant observation
  [supported] R5/r5_sequential_revoked_allow_prevented: Sequential revoked grant, wrong allow, effect prevented; not the concurrent contention loser
  [supported] R5/r5_contention_first_claim_supported: First claim under active shared grant
  [still_unverifiable] R5/r5_unbounded_population_safety: Unbounded population-scale or live BMO-mesh safety is outside the finite model — still unverifiable
  [still_unverifiable] R5/r5_concurrent_reference_loser_unmapped: The concurrent reference loser (stale at decision, settlement refused) is outside this finite model; interleavings are not in Γ
limits:
  - grant ∈ {active, revoked}
  - decision ∈ {allow, deny}
  - effect_committed ∈ {false, true}
  - ≤2 implementation arms in comparison models
  - no concurrent interleavings (see issue #10)
  - no cryptographic authenticity adversary beyond a misbind flag
